prism detector
==================

Write a function:

    def prism_detector(grid: list[str], pattern: str) -> list[tuple[int, int, str]]

Find every occurrence of `pattern` in a rectangular character grid, looking
in all 8 directions. Report each match as a tuple
(start_row, start_col, direction_code), where the start cell holds the
FIRST character of the pattern. Scan rows top to bottom, each row left to
right, and test the directions in the order listed below, so the result
order is deterministic. An empty grid or an empty pattern gives [].

Direction codes (row step, column step):
    "H"   ( 0,  1)  left to right       "H-"  ( 0, -1)  right to left
    "V"   ( 1,  0)  top to bottom       "V-"  (-1,  0)  bottom to top
    "D1"  ( 1,  1)  down-right          "D1-" (-1, -1)  up-left
    "D2"  ( 1, -1)  down-left           "D2-" (-1,  1)  up-right

Examples:
    prism_detector(["ABC", "DEF", "GHI"], "ADG") -> [(0, 0, 'V')]
    prism_detector(["XYZ", "ABC", "DEF"], "XBF") -> [(0, 0, 'D1')]
    prism_detector(["AB", "BA"], "AB") -> [(0, 0, 'H'), (0, 0, 'V'), (1, 1, 'H-'), (1, 1, 'V-')]
    prism_detector(["HELLO", "WORLD"], "LL") -> [(0, 2, 'H'), (0, 2, 'D1'), (0, 3, 'H-'), (0, 3, 'V'), (1, 3, 'V-'), (1, 3, 'D1-')]
    prism_detector([], "ABC") -> []
    prism_detector(["ABC"], "") -> []
